Today's Complete Journey: Kubernetes to Amazon EKS Production-Style Deployment

Objective:
The objective of today's activity was to move from a local Kubernetes learning setup to a real Amazon EKS deployment and understand how production-style Kubernetes components work together. We deployed a two-tier Flask + MySQL application on Amazon EKS using Kubernetes YAML manifests, persistent EBS storage, AWS Load Balancer Controller, ALB Ingress, HPA, ConfigMaps, Secrets, and supporting AWS IAM permissions.

