5. EKS API Permission Issue and Fix
====================================================================

While creating the EKS cluster, the following error occurred:

AccessDeniedException:
User is not authorized to perform:
eks:DescribeClusterVersions

Additional command also failed:

aws eks list-clusters

Root Cause:
The EC2 IAM role was authenticated, but did not have enough EKS API permissions.

Fix:
Created a customer-managed IAM policy with EKS full access.

Policy:

{
"Version": "2012-10-17",
"Statement": [
{
"Effect": "Allow",
"Action": [
"eks:*"
],
"Resource": "*"
}
]
}

Attached this policy to:

EKS-Admin-Role

Validation after fix:

aws eks describe-cluster-versions

This command started working after the custom EKS policy was attached.

Learning:
AWS authentication and AWS authorization are different.

Authentication:
aws sts get-caller-identity works

Authorization:
Specific AWS API permissions are still required.

