16. EBS CSI Controller CrashLoopBackOff
====================================================================

Checked EBS CSI pods:

kubectl get pods -n kube-system | grep ebs

Output:

ebs-csi-controller CrashLoopBackOff
ebs-csi-node Running

Controller logs:

kubectl logs -n kube-system <ebs-csi-controller-pod> -c ebs-plugin --tail=100

Error:

UnauthorizedOperation:
User is not authorized to perform:
ec2:DescribeAvailabilityZones

Role in error:

eksctl-demo-eks-nodegroup-worker-n-NodeInstanceRole-aExYouLwlh43

Root Cause:
The worker node IAM role did not have sufficient EC2 permissions required by the EBS CSI controller.

====================================================================
17. Fixed Worker Node IAM Permissions
====================================================================

Checked worker node role:

aws iam list-roles | grep NodeInstanceRole

Role found:

eksctl-demo-eks-nodegroup-worker-n-NodeInstanceRole-aExYouLwlh43

Checked attached policies:

aws iam list-attached-role-policies \
--role-name eksctl-demo-eks-nodegroup-worker-n-NodeInstanceRole-aExYouLwlh43

Initially attached policies:

AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore
AmazonEKS_CNI_Policy
AmazonEKSWorkerNodePolicy
AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryPullOnly

Fix:
Attached AmazonEC2FullAccess to the worker node IAM role.

After this, EBS CSI controller was able to create EBS volumes.

