32. ALB 404 Issue and Explanation
====================================================================

When using a host-based ingress rule such as:

two-tier-app.local

and browsing the ALB DNS directly, ALB may return:

HTTP 404

Reason:
ALB receives this Host header:

k8s-default-twotiera-d05012e3b8-875215614.ap-southeast-2.elb.amazonaws.com

but the Ingress rule expects:

two-tier-app.local

Fix options:

Option 1:
Remove host from ingress rule so any host header is accepted.

Option 2:
Use the correct Host header:

curl -H "Host: two-tier-app.local" http://<ALB-DNS>

Option 3:
Create a Route53 DNS record:

two-tier-app.local
↓
ALB DNS

For learning, removing the host rule is simpler.

