40. ECR
====================================================================

Amazon ECR (Elastic Container Registry) – Complete Notes

1. Objective

The objective of this activity was to learn Amazon Elastic Container Registry (ECR) and integrate it with Amazon EKS.

Amazon ECR is AWS's fully managed private container registry used to store, manage, version, and deploy Docker container images.

Target Architecture:

Docker Build
↓
Amazon ECR
↓
Amazon EKS
↓
Pods

====================================================================

2. Why Amazon ECR?

Before ECR:

Developer
↓
Docker Hub
↓
Amazon EKS

After ECR:

Developer
↓
Amazon ECR
↓
Amazon EKS

Benefits:

- Fully managed AWS service
- Private image registry
- IAM-based authentication
- Native integration with EKS
- No Docker Hub rate limits
- Image versioning support
- Lifecycle policy support
- Improved security

====================================================================

3. Initial Access Issue

Command:

